# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is **already installed and properly configured** in this Next.js project. No changes were necessary.

## Findings

### 1. Package Installation ✅
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1`
- **Status**: Already present in `package.json` dependencies
- **Package Manager**: pnpm (confirmed by presence of `pnpm-lock.yaml`)

### 2. Analytics Configuration ✅
- **File**: `frontend/app/layout.tsx`
- **Import**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- **Component**: `<Analytics />` properly placed within the `<body>` element of the root layout

### 3. Framework Verification ✅
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router)
- **Configuration**: Follows official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router exactly
- **Documentation Source**: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart (fetched June 6, 2026)

### 4. Verification Tests Performed ✅
- ✅ Dependencies installed successfully with `pnpm install`
- ✅ Build completed successfully with `pnpm build`
- ✅ No new errors introduced (linter shows pre-existing errors unrelated to Analytics)
- ✅ No test script available in package.json (none to run)

## Implementation Details

The project follows the exact setup from the official Vercel documentation:

**Next.js App Router Setup:**
```typescript
// app/layout.tsx
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This implementation is complete and ready for production. Once deployed to Vercel, analytics will automatically start tracking page views and can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section.

## Next Steps for the Project Owner

1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**: Navigate to your project's Analytics section and click "Enable" if not already done
2. **Deploy**: Run `vercel deploy` to push to production
3. **Verify**: Check browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view` after deployment
4. **Dashboard**: Access analytics data through the Vercel project dashboard

## Notes
- No files were modified as the setup was already complete
- The configuration matches the latest Vercel documentation (verified June 6, 2026)
- The Analytics component is properly placed at the end of the body for optimal performance
